# Golden proposal development lock

The **Golden** proposal (`residential_executive`, Executive Premium editorial renderer) is **complete and locked for development**.

## What "locked" means

- **Do NOT** modify Golden proposal files when fixing or building **other** presets (Sales Premium, Ember, Horizon, Solstice, Legacy, Commercial, etc.).
- **Do NOT** hide or disable other themes in the UI — users may still choose any template.
- **Only** edit Golden when the user **explicitly** asks to change the Golden proposal.

## Frozen paths (no edits unless user requests Golden changes)

- `components/proposals/executive-premium-editorial/**`
- `lib/executive-premium-editorial/**`
- `components/proposals/executive-premium-nextgen/executive-premium-nextgen-renderer.tsx`

See also `lib/golden-proposal-lock.ts`.

## When working on other presets

- Scope diffs to that preset's blocks, CSS, and registry entries only.
- Do not refactor shared Golden utilities (`transform-to-editorial-model`, `ep-golden-i18n`, etc.) for another theme's sake — duplicate or adapt in the other preset's folder if needed.
- `ember-golden` / `horizon-golden` blocks may **read** editorial models; do not change Golden pages/CSS to match them.

## Public route

Golden renders at `preset_id === "residential_executive"` via `ExecutivePremiumEditorialRenderer` — keep that path stable.
